\n- **Pull request:** #101, against `main`. The first attempt to open it timed out, but the PR had been created without reviewers. I checked the open PRs to avoid a duplicate, then requested review from alex on #101 directly. I did not cancel and recreate it.\n\nMerging into main still needs code-owner approval under org policy, so #101 is waiting on review.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the failing test and the module it covers.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01H3MBhQSVxcFRBkx1vHAZke", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Jj7opcijGDtbrjSbnWAoxw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP` while its docstring and the test expect `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Both test cases check out under half-even (2.675 \u2192 2.68 since 7 is odd; 2.665 \u2192 2.66 since 6 is even). I'll create a branch and make the fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01STfkJ3eRJxzZLkVbr8Yyyr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01H1fVHABBmxDC8viVqPcyKZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is committed to the branch. Next I'll start CI on it and wait for the result.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016YKkc2z3zZiGYgBLUdEPvC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016vvYkgcrigfSV791Metfgh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986. Next I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01EKxYwPUW4pSrk25cYpChef", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "Fixes the nightly build failure in tests/test_money.py.\n\n`round_money` in src/money.py was using `ROUND_HALF_UP`, while its docstring and FIN-212 require banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). This changes the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. No other behavior changes.\n\nCI: passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so I don't know whether the PR was created. I'll check the open PRs before retrying, to avoid opening a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01